{"id": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java::31::0", "file": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java", "module": "spring-websocket", "block_start": 31, "start": 32, "end": 34, "indent": "", "lines": ["Represents a WebSocket extension as defined in the RFC 6455.", "WebSocket extensions add protocol features to the WebSocket protocol. The extensions", "used within a session are negotiated during the handshake phase as follows:"]}
{"id": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java::31::1", "file": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java", "module": "spring-websocket", "block_start": 31, "start": 40, "end": 41, "indent": "", "lines": ["<p>WebSocket Extension HTTP headers may include parameters and follow", "<a href=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7230#section-3.2\">RFC 7230 section 3.2</a></p>"]}
{"id": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java::31::2", "file": "spring-websocket/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/socket/WebSocketExtension.java", "module": "spring-websocket", "block_start": 31, "start": 43, "end": 44, "indent": "", "lines": ["<p>Note that the order of extensions in HTTP headers defines their order of execution,", "e.g. extensions \"foo, bar\" will be executed as \"bar(foo(message))\".</p>"]}
